    "text": "\n000\nFXUS65 KVEF 242314\nAFDVEF\n\nArea Forecast Discussion\nNational Weather Service Las Vegas NV\n414 PM PDT Sat Oct 24 2026\n\n.KEY MESSAGES...\n\n* Gusty north winds will decrease throughout the afternoon with \n  lingering shower and storm chances in northwestern Arizona.\n\n* Quiet and seasonable conditions through at least Wednesday, with\n  signs of a more active pattern returning late in the week.\n\n&&\n\n.DISCUSSION...Today through Friday.\n\nEarly afternoon infrared and water vapor satellite imagery shows \nelongated troughing across the Southwestern US from the shortwave \nthat dropped into the area last night. This shortwave was \nresponsible for the overnight uptick in north winds across the \nregion. These winds will gradually decrease throughout the afternoon. \n In addition to breezy north winds, Mohave County will see isolated \nshowers and thunderstorms as this trough lingers across the area \ntoday. For the most part precipitation will be light. However, with \nthe cold air aloft and lingering moisture, stronger storms will be \ncapable of producing moderate-to-heavy rain. Nuisance flooding and \nisolated instances of flash flooding will be possible. \n\nWeather will calm down heading into next week as the trough exits on \nSunday. Dry conditions and seasonable temperatures are on tap for \nthe first half of the week. Guidance continues to show the weather \npattern becoming more active late next week as the subtropical jet \ndraws moisture into the Southwestern US. Cluster analysis shows \nseveral variations of offshore troughing during this time, so there \nremains a fair amount of uncertainty, but there appears to be a good \nsignal for the existence of an offshore trough and southwesterly \nflow over us. Should this come to fruition, we should see an \nincrease in southwest winds and low to moderate (10-50%) \nprecipitation chances around Halloween weekend.\n&&\n\n\n.AVIATION...For Harry Reid...For the 00Z Forecast Package...Best \nchances of vicinity showers between 00Z and 02Z, with a 40 percent \nchance of gusty winds from their direction between 20 and 30 kts and \nrain over the terminal. Northerly winds will continue to gradually \nsubside through the remainder of the afternoon. Gusts should cease \naround 00Z. Expect directional variability between 330 and 030 \nthrough the day today. Overnight, winds will become light and \nvariable before becoming light and east-northeasterly Sunday \nafternoon. \n\nFor the rest of southern Nevada, northwest Arizona and southeast \nCalifornia...For the 00Z Forecast Package...Northerly wind gusts \nbetween 25 and 30 kts will continue to subside through the day at \nLas Vegas Valley and Colorado River Valley TAF sites. KBIH will \nremain north, but will range between 6 and 9 kts. KDAG will be light \nand variable. FEW-SCT aoa 10 kft will clear out through the day.\n&&\n\n\n.SPOTTER INFORMATION STATEMENT...Spotters are encouraged to report\nany significant weather or impacts according to standard operating\nprocedures.\n\n&&\n\n$$\n\nDISCUSSION...Stessman\nAVIATION...Soulat\n\nFor more forecast information...see us on our webpage:\nhttps://weather.gov/lasvegas or follow us on Facebook and Twitter\n",
